# Protect Data and Secrets

## Inputs and boundaries

- Validate untrusted input before using it in queries, file paths, commands, or external requests.
- Use parameterized APIs and appropriate encoding instead of building executable strings from input.
- Enforce existing access checks where the project has users or protected data.

## Secrets and logs

- Do not hardcode passwords, tokens, private keys, or other credentials.
- Use the project's existing secret or environment configuration method.
- Avoid logging sensitive values; redact them from errors and examples.
- Never commit real secrets or private data in test fixtures.

When changing data handling, check that the original permissions and privacy behavior still hold. Flag a discovered secret or data exposure without repeating the secret in chat or a commit.
